# GROUND ABOVE THE GROUND (docs/ABOVE.md S1-S2): a rock arch staged over the
# moss's heart with `--above=arch` (AboveStage), no worldgen. It must read as
# rock hanging in the air and not as a block: an edge that wanders like a
# terrace's, its rim the land's own strata, its top the land's own ground, its
# shadow on the ground. From above, standing under it, the arch is cut at the
# section plane (law 3): its span over the player gone and chalked, its feet
# standing with an inked cap. Then over the shoulder, from under it, looking
# along it and up at it.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/above-arch.tour --seed=1 --place=moss --above=arch --hour=10.5 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
wait 0.6
await above_cut 3
shot 01-under-the-arch-from-above-cut
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
await above_whole 3
wait 0.8
shot 02-under-the-arch-over-the-shoulder with shoulder
mouse 500,0 0.5
wait 0.8
shot 03-along-the-arch with shoulder
mouse 0,-260 0.4
wait 0.8
shot 04-up-at-its-underside with shoulder
